The second view depends on the first view.

10. Advantages and Disadvantages of Views
Advantages
1. Security

Hide sensitive columns.

2. Simplicity

Complex queries can be accessed using a simple:

SELECT * FROM ViewName;
3. Reusability

Frequently used queries can be reused.

4. Abstraction

Users dont need to understand the underlying table relationships.

5. Consistency

A common business query can have one centralized definition.

6. Reporting

Views are useful for creating reports and dashboards.

Disadvantages
1. Performance

A complex view can result in an expensive query.

2. Update limitations

Not every view is updatable.

3. Dependency

If an underlying table or column is changed or removed, the view can be affected.

4. Complex nested views

Too many views built on top of other views can make debugging and performance analysis difficult.

5. Doesnt normally store result data

A normal view generally retrieves data from the underlying tables when queried.

⭐ Simple vs Complex View
Simple View	Complex View
Usually one table	Usually multiple tables
Simple SELECT	May contain JOIN, aggregation, etc.
Easier to update	Often not directly updatable
Easy to understand	More complex
